WEBVTT

00:19:28.971 --> 00:19:30.694
RB: So I went along to one of these

00:19:30.718 --> 00:19:32.823
and one of the guys
who was leading it says,

00:19:32.847 --> 00:19:35.249
"Oh, Rachel, have you come
to observe our session?"

00:19:35.273 --> 00:19:37.431
I said, "No, I've come
to learn how to code."

00:19:37.455 --> 00:19:39.280
And he looked at me like I'd gone off.

00:19:39.304 --> 00:19:41.566
He's like, "But you're
a director in technology.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:42.757
Surely you can code."

00:19:42.781 --> 00:19:44.115
And I'm like, "No."

00:19:45.115 --> 00:19:48.645
AG: People are often afraid
to admit gaps in their expertise,

00:19:48.669 --> 00:19:51.508
but there's evidence that seeking
knowledge, help and advice

00:19:51.532 --> 00:19:54.080
can actually signal confidence
and a desire to learn.

00:19:54.589 --> 00:19:56.097
Those who use BetterUp coaching

00:19:56.121 --> 00:19:59.349
report significant increases
in confidence and resilience.

00:19:59.373 --> 00:20:01.472
By working with Victoria
to shift her mindset